Source material. The divinatory wording is quoted from Arthur Edward Waite
(1857-1942), The Pictorial Key to the Tarot (London: William Rider & Son,
1911; text of the 1922 reprint). The Golden Dawn titles and attributions are
taken from The Equinox, vol. I, no. 8 (London: Wieland & Co., 1912). Both
works were published before 1931 and are in the public domain in the United
States; their authors died more than 70 years ago, so they are also in the
public domain in the European Union and the United Kingdom. The titles and
attributions are historical facts. This license covers StarTarot's selection,
normalization, organization and original documentation only; it claims no new
exclusive rights in the public-domain material. Reusers remain responsible for
checking the law of any other jurisdiction.

Attribution must not suggest that A. E. Waite, the Golden Dawn, the source
publishers, or StarTarot endorses a reuse or its conclusions.
